WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.920
Let's get into exactly how chest compressions are done.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.840
Everything starts with your hands.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:11.100
Look at the screen and watch your instructor, because getting your hand placement right

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.040
is the foundation of high quality CPR.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:18.040
First, you want to find the center of the person's chest.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:23.520
You are going to place the heel of one hand directly on the lower half of the breast bone,

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.320
which is also called the sternum.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:30.379
This is the strongest part of the chest, and it is right where the heart is waiting for

00:00:30.379 --> 00:00:31.920
that manual pump.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:37.360
Next, take your other hand and place the heel of it right on top of the first one.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:40.080
From there, lace your fingers together.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.560
Lacing your fingers helps keep your hands focused on that center spot so they do not

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:46.680
slide around while you are working.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:49.560
The final part of your setup is your posture.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:53.320
You need to keep your arms straight and lock your elbows.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:57.080
Position yourself so your shoulders are directly over your hands.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:01.320
By doing this, you are not just using your arm muscles to push.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:04.660
You are using your entire upper body weight to do the work.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.139
It is much more effective and less tiring for you.

00:01:08.139 --> 00:01:12.080
Take a moment now to get into this position over your mannequin.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:16.959
Feel that alignment from your shoulders all the way down to the heel of your hand.

00:01:16.959 --> 00:01:20.760
Once you have that locked in, we are ready to move on to the actual push.

